# dist/loader.js is a minified single-line build artifact. Git's text merge
# produces a file that matches neither side, and that file is what jsDelivr
# serves to ~164 live pages.
#
# `-merge` makes git refuse to merge it and leave a conflict instead. Resolve
# by taking either side; .githooks/pre-commit rebuilds it from src on the
# resolving commit, so the content is correct either way.
#
# This replaced `merge=auto-rebuild` on 10 Sep 2026. That named a merge driver
# nothing defined — drivers live in .git/config, which is not version
# controlled — so the attribute was a no-op and git text-merged the bundle.
dist/loader.js -merge
